##
## Cross-sign anchors for the ESP32 modules' certificate bundle
##
## Roots that Mozilla no longer trusts for TLS but that chains servers send today still
## need. ESP-IDF v5.3's bundle check (esp_crt_verify_callback) looks up only the issuer of
## the topmost certificate a server sends, and tries no other path, so a server that sends an
## intermediate cross-signed by a dropped root fails even when the newer root is in
## cacert.pem. ESP-IDF builds the bundle from this directory: cacert.pem and this file.
##
## Only roots a measured host needs are here. Of the 17 dropped roots with a still-valid
## cross-certificate to a current root (CCADB, 2026-09-29), no host among 316 measured needed
## the other 13, and Entrust Root Certification Authority - G2 is never anchored: Mozilla
## distrusted Entrust for cause.
##
## A reviewed commit changes this file, followed by `python3 tools/ca_store/ca_store.py pin`,
## which moves CA_ANCHORS_SHA256 and CA_BUNDLE_SET_SHA256 and bumps the modules that attach the
## bundle. No tool changes it on its own. The tests (tools/ca_store/test_ca_store.py) fail when
## an anchor has expired, or when no recorded chain (tools/ca_store/test_chains.pem) that has
## not itself expired needs it, so each anchor is removed when its cross-signs run out, or
## when the chains are recorded again and no server sends one any more. The file ends with a
## certificate.
##
## Each anchor is retired for good by ESP-IDF 6.x with
## CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE_CROSS_SIGNED_VERIFY enabled (it defaults to off), which
## checks a cross-signed chain against the newer root instead.
##

## Why:
##   Google Trust Services serves GTS Root R4 and GTS Root R1 cross-signed by this root, and
##   GlobalSign serves R3, R5 and R46 the same way; one host sends the root itself. All of
##   those cross-signs run to 2028-01-28. Anchoring it trusts everything still issued under
##   it, not only the cross-signs.
## Needed by (80 hosts measured 2026-09-29, of 316 that answered):
##   1541u-documentation.readthedocs.io, adtrafficquality.google, aliyuncs.com,
##   api.anthropic.com, api.coinbase.com, api.ipify.org, api.mistral.ai, api.openai.com,
##   app-analytics-services.com, app-measurement.com, applovin.com, base.org, blogspot.com,
##   cdn.discordapp.com, chatgpt.com, cloudflare.com, commodore.net,
##   commoserve.files.commodore.net, creativecommons.org, discord.com, discord.gg,
##   dns.google, docs.google.com, doubleclick.net, drive.google.com, fonts.googleapis.com,
##   forms.gle, forum64.de, gateway.discord.gg, generativelanguage.googleapis.com,
##   godaddy.com, goo.gl, google-analytics.com, google.com, googleadservices.com,
##   googleapis.com, googledomains.com, googlesyndication.com, googletagmanager.com,
